## Public cloud

A public cloud is a type of cloud computing service that provides resources and services over the internet to multiple users and organizations. It is called "public" because the cloud infrastructure is owned and operated by a third-party cloud service provider and is made available to the general public or a wide range of customers. These cloud providers typically have vast data centers with a multitude of servers, storage, and networking equipment that they use to deliver various cloud services.

